      "title": "8.7.1 Homogeneous equilibrium",
      "language": "en",
      "source_refs": [
        {
          "source_document_id": "b07b1f6c-f5a4-509d-ae86-73be5bffb0d4",
          "pdf_from": 172,
          "pdf_to": 173,
          "note": "Topic 8.7.1 with the unnumbered Heterogeneous Equilibrium section, printed pages 172-173, and Quick Check 8.3."
        }
      ],
      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "An equilibrium system in which all of the reactants and products are in the same phase. The following are examples of homogeneous equilibria:"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{N2_{(g)} + 3H2_{(g)} <=> 2NH3_{(g)}}",
            "text_alt": "N₂(g) + 3H₂(g) ⇌ 2NH₃(g)"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{2SO2_{(g)} + O2_{(g)} <=> 2SO3_{(g)}}",
            "text_alt": "2SO₂(g) + O₂(g) ⇌ 2SO₃(g)"
          },
          {
            "type": "equation",
            "latex": "\\ce{CH3COOH_{(l)} + C2H5OH_{(l)} <=> CH3COOC2H5_{(l)} + H2O_{(l)}}",
            "text_alt": "CH₃COOH(l) + C₂H₅OH(l) ⇌ CH₃COOC₂H₅(l) + H₂O(l)"
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
